[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824111603","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105670#issuecomment-2824111603","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105670","id":2824111603,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oVIXz","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-23T12:23:43Z","updated_at":"2025-04-23T12:23:43Z","body":"WebXR almost certainly doesn't work with wasm64 because of the way we're passing data between JS and C++. But that's something that I'll need to work on in a future PR :-)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824111603/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824496102","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105670#issuecomment-2824496102","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105670","id":2824496102,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oWmPm","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-23T14:24:22Z","updated_at":"2025-04-23T14:25:07Z","body":"I modified my PR to remove `WASM_MEMORY64_ENABLED` and to introduce instead a runtime check instead:\r\n```cpp\r\n// in `platform/web/os_main.h`\r\nbool is_memory64() const { return sizeof(size_t) == sizeof(uint64_t); }\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824496102/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824510366","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105670#issuecomment-2824510366","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105670","id":2824510366,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oWpue","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-23T14:28:49Z","updated_at":"2025-04-23T14:28:49Z","body":"> I modified my PR to remove `WASM_MEMORY64_ENABLED` and to introduce instead a runtime check instead:\r\n\r\nIf we can know at compile time, why use a runtime check?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824510366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824538133","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105670#issuecomment-2824538133","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105670","id":2824538133,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oWwgV","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-23T14:37:51Z","updated_at":"2025-04-23T14:53:06Z","body":"> > I modified my PR to remove `WASM_MEMORY64_ENABLED` and to introduce instead a runtime check instead:\r\n> \r\n> If we can know at compile time, why use a runtime check?\r\n\r\nYeah. That's a compelling argument. But I could force inlining the function and the optimizer will surely optimize the crap out of these static checks.\r\n\r\nI'm just worried to introduce a `#define` that essentially does a simple `sizeof()` check can do.\r\n\r\nEdit: I just did add `_FORCE_INLINE_` to the function.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824538133/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824677660","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105670#issuecomment-2824677660","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105670","id":2824677660,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oXSkc","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-23T15:22:33Z","updated_at":"2025-04-23T15:22:33Z","body":"I put the PR in draft mode for the following reason. I just realized that we append the builds with `.wasm32` currently. \r\n\r\n<img width=\"461\" alt=\"Capture d’écran, le 2025-04-23 à 11 20 35\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/65c9aab8-34a5-4565-b356-e5c1ccc13525\" />\r\n\r\nAs `memory64=wasm64` is technically not strictly compatible/interchangeable with `wasm32`, I wonder if we should change the build prefix to be `wasm64` instead of `wasm32`. It complicates everything though, buildsystem-wise. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824677660/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824766667","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105670#issuecomment-2824766667","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105670","id":2824766667,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oXoTL","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-23T15:51:01Z","updated_at":"2025-04-23T15:51:28Z","body":"> But I could force inlining the function and the optimizer will surely optimize the crap out of these static checks.\r\n\r\nMy usual inclination is to not trust the compiler. :-) But this isn't my area of expertise, so I'm happy to trust more knowledgeable folks\r\n\r\n> As `memory64=wasm64` is technically not strictly compatible/interchangeable with `wasm32`, I wonder if we should change the build prefix to be `wasm64` instead of `wasm32`.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I think, yes, these should use the suffix `wasm64` (and probably `wasm32+64bitptrs` too?)\r\n\r\nI think we'll also need feature tags for these different types, because I think GDExtensions will also need to be compiled the same way as Godot in order to work together, and we'll need a way for Godot to select the right binary. Example:\r\n\r\n```\r\nweb.debug.wasm32 = \"res://bin/libgdexample.web.template_debug.wasm32.nothreads.wasm\"\r\nweb.release.wasm32 = \"res://bin/libgdexample.web.template_release.wasm32.nothreads.wasm\"\r\nweb.debug.wasm64 = \"res://bin/libgdexample.web.template_debug.wasm64.nothreads.wasm\"\r\nweb.release.wasm64 = \"res://bin/libgdexample.web.template_release.wasm64.nothreads.wasm\"\r\nweb.debug.wasm32+64bitptrs = \"res://bin/libgdexample.web.template_debug.wasm32+64bitptrs.nothreads.wasm\"\r\nweb.release.wasm32+64bitptrs = \"res://bin/libgdexample.web.template_release.wasm32+64bitptrs.nothreads.wasm\"\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824766667/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824909944","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105670#issuecomment-2824909944","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105670","id":2824909944,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oYLR4","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-23T16:42:33Z","updated_at":"2025-04-23T16:43:40Z","body":"> (and probably `wasm32+64bitptrs` too?)\r\n\r\nTechnically, `wasm32+64bitptrs` should work on modern browsers, even on Safari (which don't support MEMORY64). So maybe we could stick to `wasm32` for those builds.\r\n\r\nEdit: OH. GDExtensions, right. Forgot about this. I will test the compatibility between them.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2824909944/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4339115308","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105670#issuecomment-4339115308","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105670","id":4339115308,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAqGlLA","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-28T21:15:52Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T21:15:52Z","body":"What is the relationship between this PR and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102378? Does PR #102378 supersede this?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"ur